    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "334526fb-7d8d-8042-a456-d9c796e5f793",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2f5526fb-7d8d-80f1-bb45-d3289ae0df93"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-03-31T17:30:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-04-29T01:47:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "a1863291-3f2b-499c-99b9-789ceec151cc"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "245d872b-594c-8106-8297-0002b46a489f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "This course is an entry point into The Laboratory for Cybernetics (Lab4C) in Carnegie Mellon—Architecture for those who see themselves committing to exploring responses to “wicked challenges”—for example but not limited to social justice, climate change, artificial intelligence, three pillars of the CM—ARCHITECTURE Pedagogy—in the context of vast ambiguities and unpredictabilities of our 21st-century world.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "This course is an entry point into The Laboratory for Cybernetics (Lab4C) in Carnegie Mellon—Architecture for those who see themselves committing to exploring responses to “wicked challenges”—for example but not limited to social justice, climate change, artificial intelligence, three pillars of the CM—ARCHITECTURE Pedagogy—in the context of vast ambiguities and unpredictabilities of our 21st-century world.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      },
      "archived": false
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "334526fb-7d8d-801a-8313-f90399794265",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2f5526fb-7d8d-80f1-bb45-d3289ae0df93"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-03-31T17:30:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-04-29T01:50:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "a1863291-3f2b-499c-99b9-789ceec151cc"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "245d872b-594c-8106-8297-0002b46a489f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Embracing ambiguity, critical thinking, and experimental creativity, Lab4C supports students and researchers grappling with wicked challenges by offering concepts and materials, models and methods from Cybernetics and Systems. Lab4C also offers connections to potential collaborators through its network of in-world practitioners.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Embracing ambiguity, critical thinking, and experimental creativity, Lab4C supports students and researchers grappling with wicked challenges by offering concepts and materials, models and methods from Cybernetics and Systems. Lab4C also offers connections to potential collaborators through its network of in-world practitioners.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      },
      "archived": false
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "334526fb-7d8d-80b6-a3f8-d34fc33489ba",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "2f5526fb-7d8d-80f1-bb45-d3289ae0df93"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-03-31T17:30:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-04-29T01:47:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "a1863291-3f2b-499c-99b9-789ceec151cc"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "245d872b-594c-8106-8297-0002b46a489f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "The trans-discipline of Cybernetics offers concepts, models, and methods for approaching complex adaptive systems of any makeup from the perspectives of purpose—the purpose attributed to the system and the purpose of those who articulate the system’s purpose. Cybernetics is unique because it demands both humane-based explanations for how systems behave as well as responsibility for our own behavior in how we encounter, delimit, interact with, and explain those systems.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "The trans-discipline of Cybernetics offers concepts, models, and methods for approaching complex adaptive systems of any makeup from the perspectives of purpose—the purpose attributed to the system and the purpose of those who articulate the system’s purpose. Cybernetics is unique because it demands both humane-based explanations for how systems behave as well as responsibility for our own behavior in how we encounter, delimit, interact with, and explain those systems.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      },
      "archived": false
    },
